// Pirate: meson vision - ported from space-wizards/space-station-14#44601 ("Mesons (XRayVision)").
//
// Upstream's version also samples the engine FOV shadow-depth map here and discards every fragment that is
// actually visible, and tints what survives with its own color/scanlines. The FOV sampling needs
// IClydeViewport.FovRenderTarget (RobustToolbox#6781), which our pinned engine does not have, so that test
// happens per-tile on the CPU in XRayVisionOverlay.IsHidden instead. The hue and scanlines were dropped by
// request - revealed tiles are meant to read as the same color as the rest of the screen (tinted uniformly by
// the goggles' full-screen shader, see SharedXRayVisionSystem.SetEnabled), not a separately-colored patch.
//
// So this shader is a deliberate passthrough. It exists ONLY for the light_mode line below; the brightness
// that upstream folded into its tint alpha is now a neutral white modulate on the draw call instead
// (XRayVisionComponent.TileAlpha), which dims without tinting.

// Anything revealed here is outside FOV and therefore in darkness by definition - without this the lighting
// pass blackens it straight back out. This is also exactly why revealed tiles need TileAlpha to dim them:
// skipping the lighting pass means skipping the dimming that everything else on screen receives, so they
// would otherwise glare at full texture brightness.
light_mode unshaded;

void fragment()
{
    COLOR = zTexture(UV);
}
